1
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:11,000
No accidents. No coincidences. No escapes. You can't cheat death.

2
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Final Destination is a horror film directed by James Wong.

3
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:21,000
After a teenager has a terrifying vision of him and his friends dying in a plane crash,
he prevents the accident only to have Death hunt them down, one by one.

4
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Alex Browning, played by Devon Sawa.

5
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Clear Rivers, played by Ali Larter.

6
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:36,000
Carter Horton, played by Kerr Smith.

7
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:41,000
Valerie Lewton, played by Kristen Cloke.

8
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Agent Weine, played by Daniel Roebuck.

9
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Agent Schreck, played by Roger Guenveur Smith.

10
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:56,000
Final Destination is a 2000 American supernatural horror film directed by James Wong (in his directorial debut),
who co-wrote the screenplay with Glen Morgan and Jeffrey Reddick, based on a story by Reddick.

11
00:44:55,000 --> 00:45:01,000
It stars Devon Sawa, Ali Larter, Kerr Smith, and Tony Todd.

12
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:06,000
Sawa portrays a teenager who cheats death after having a
premonition of a catastrophic plane explosion.

13
00:53:05,000 --> 00:53:11,000
He and several of his classmates leave the plane before the explosion occurs, but
Death later takes the lives of those who were meant to die on the plane.

14
00:57:10,000 --> 00:57:16,000
The film began as a spec script written by Reddick for an episode of
The X-Files in order for Reddick to get a TV agent.

15
01:01:15,000 --> 01:01:21,000
A colleague at New Line Cinema persuaded Reddick to
write it as a feature-length film.

16
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:26,000
Later, Wong and Morgan, The X-Files writing partners, became
interested in the script and agreed to work on the film.

17
01:09:25,000 --> 01:09:31,000
Principal photography took place in New York City and Vancouver, with
additional scenes filmed in Toronto and San Francisco.

18
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
Final Destination was released in the United States on March 17, 2000.

19
01:17:35,000 --> 01:17:41,000
The film achieved commercial success, earning $112.9
million against a $23 million budget.

20
01:21:40,000 --> 01:21:46,000
While it received mixed reviews from critics, it won the Saturn Award for Best Horror Film and Best Performance by a Younger Actor for Sawa, The film's
popularity led to the expansion of the Final Destination franchise, which includes five additional films, as well as novels and comic books.

21
01:25:45,000 --> 01:25:51,000
The first sequel, Final Destination 2, was released on January 31, 2003.

22
01:29:50,000 --> 01:29:56,000
The film explores themes of airport, time travel,
omen, premonition, airplane accident.

23
01:33:55,000 --> 01:34:01,000
The tone is dark.
